			"Message": "feat(Project): Eliminate startup visual flash and add compiled debug profiles\n\nCoordinate startup sequence improvements across Mountain, Sky, and Wind to eliminate the \"purple/dark flash\" and panel-pop flicker observed on cold boot:\n\n- **Mountain:** Implement hidden-until-ready window pattern using WebviewWindowBuilder.visible(false), reveal only when Sky reports phase 3 (Restored). Add 3s safety timer to force-reveal if Sky crashes before phase 3 (prevents invisible-window lockup).\n- **Sky:** Add missing SkyBridge initialization to Electron Layout to subscribe to cel:* Tauri events (tree-view, SCM, debug, extensions). Previously, panels painted empty on first frame then re-rendered with data.\n- **Wind:** Add PostHogDefines to TargetConfig.ts mapping LAND_POSTHOG_* environment variables to esbuild define directives, completing the hardcoded-key removal work.\n\nAdditionally, add two new debug profiles for single-binary embedded resource testing:\n- `debug-electron-compiled` - Electron workbench with all Sky/Output assets embedded via Tauri's resource table, preserving debug symbols and dev-log tags\n- `debug-mountain-compiled` - Same embedded-resource layout on the lighter Mountain workbench\n\nAlso update turbo.json to declare global dependencies (.env files) and globalEnv variables (LAND_POSTHOG_*, Product*, Tier*, etc.) for proper cache invalidation.\n\nImpact: Eliminates four-repaint startup cascade. All panels now render with data on first paint.",
